│     I fixed the ZWJ edge cases in `rich/cells.py`, and the patch is submitted (1 file changed). I did not read issues #3947 or #3950, since    │
│ the environment has no network access and I had no local copy. The fix is based on reproducing the edge cases directly.                        │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     - **`_cell_len`**: a trailing ZWJ no longer raises `StopIteration`; `next(iter_characters, None)` is used instead.                         │
│     - **`split_graphemes`**: a ZWJ after a grapheme extends its span with the index clamped to the string length, so the span can't run past   │
│ the end. A ZWJ with no preceding grapheme now advances by one character rather than two.                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     Checked by hand: `"a\u200d"` gives width 1, `"\u200d"` gives 0, `"❤️\u200d🔥"` gives 2, and the family-emoji ZWJ sequence gives 2.         │
│ `tests/test_cells.py` passes (54 tests). I did not add new tests.                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     Two things remain unverified. A leading ZWJ followed by a visible character (`"\u200da"`) still swallows that character, as the original   │
